Do these run in sequence, in the implementation? I.e. with two separate tree traversals? Or do you traverse the tree and do both at once?

The difference would be observable in the following way:

```html
<details>
<div hidden=until-found onbeforematch=test()>
Search for me using find-in-page
</div>
</details>

<script>
function test(event) {
  if (event.target.parentElement.hasAttribute("open")) {
    // The ancestor details revealing algorithm was run to completion first,
    // like the spec says.
  } else {
    // We fired beforematch before doing the full ancestor details revealing
    // algorithm.
  }
}
</script>
```

